id: pm-vcs-8xis
title: Design committed repository links local layers and typed obliteration
description: "Add native repository composition and lifecycle operations: committed links pin authorized repository and revision identities, local layers overlay an instance without changing commits, and authorized obliteration produces a typed payload state distinct from garbage collection, missing data or corruption."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-01T19:32:34.077Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-10T08:51:21.741Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 1800
acceptance_criteria: Committed links are reproducible and retain the linked repository authorization boundary; Local layers never alter commit identity and are visibly excluded from ordinary status; Obliteration is authorized audited and scoped by stable file identity; Checkout and verify distinguish obliterated content from missing and corrupt objects
parent: pm-vcs-b7cb
risk: high
comments[78]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-12T23:35:59.709Z",pi-agent,"Audit 2026-09-13: EXISTS — committed repository links are implemented as sparse linked instances (engine/instances.ts: instance link, shared object store, sparse views; test/instances.test.ts: 'a linked instance materializes its view, shares objects and keeps private state', 'concurrent instances share objects but never overwrite each other's state'). REMAINS — local layers that overlay an instance without changing commit identity are not implemented (grep for local-layer/overlay returns no matches). Typed obliteration is not implemented (grep for obliterate/Obliteration in engine/ returns no matches). Checkout and verify distinguishing obliterated content from missing and corrupt objects is not implemented. Two of four acceptance criteria are not met."
  "2026-10-07T20:55:16.467Z",codex-sol,"Baseline against the built package and a real disposable SDK tracker: a synthetic binary was staged and committed successfully; vcs link, vcs layer and vcs obliterate are absent, and the repository exposes no layer or obliteration API. Acceptance will pin a typed external repository revision and subset across a clone without transferring its payload or credentials; overlay tracked and new paths while preserving commit identity and excluding layers visibly from status and add; authorize FileId-scoped erasure across moves and revisions, byte-scan stored and decoded representations, distinguish obliterated/missing/corrupt state, and reject resurrection through stale fetch/import. The previous audit conflated local shared instances with committed external links. Full item, parent, linked research record and LORE.md were read; the removed historical research-doc link is superseded by LORE.md."
  "2026-10-07T20:56:24.216Z",codex-sol,"Design recorded first in docs/links-layers-obliteration.md: canonical typed committed links with explicit target authorization; private layer snapshots masked from staging/status and preserved across materialization; authorized FileId erasure with durable typed denial, full-store historical inventory, deduplication refusal, byte removal and non-resurrection at every object arrival boundary. Remote tombstones cannot silently authorize deletion of locally held content. Verification and checkout preserve the distinction between intentional erasure, missing data and corruption."
  "2026-10-07T21:01:09.761Z",codex-sol-implementation,"Implementation decision: typed link leaf objects carry only repository identity, exact commit ID and explicit file mappings. Resolution requires a separately authorized local target binding and creates a private layer. Layers preserve edited disk bytes across materialization and refuse removal without explicit edit discard. Erasure inventories all loose objects, indexes and registered instances under one store writer lock; unknown pack/cache artefacts and deduplication conflicts refuse before denial. Durable pending denial blocks all writes until authorized cleanup completes. After erasure, resumable payload-only batches refuse because they carry no FileId provenance; complete bundles preflight every tree and payload before publication."
  "2026-10-07T21:18:28.147Z",codex-sol,"Independent adversarial review found a closure-validation defect in the feature candidate: a canonical forged payload tombstone for an absent commit allowed a bundle to publish a ref and verification to report intentional absence with no missing/corrupt failure. Required correction: only FileId-attributed payload leaves may be obliterated; commits, parent commits and trees must remain present and correctly typed. Add refusal tests that assert no ref publication, including mismatched leaf FileId denial. Independent real-tracker overlay checks passed for restore, view narrowing and conflicting merge preservation."
  "2026-10-07T21:23:32.566Z",codex-sol-implementation,"Adversarial review exposed a role-confusion bug: denial addresses were accepted for absent commits or trees. Implementing one context-aware closure validator for publication and verification, requiring correctly typed structure and matching FileId/root attribution at intentionally absent payload leaves. Import preflight will validate before storage or ref publication. Canonical audit objects are reconstructed from received denial metadata for fresh clones."
  "2026-10-07T21:26:31.396Z",codex-sol-implementation,"Role-aware closure regressions pass: absent denied refs/parents/trees and unrelated FileId leaves are refused before objects or refs publish. Fresh clones retain canonical tombstone audit objects and verify them outside the tree closure. Four real processes converge on one identity; empty clones preserve source identity. npm package.files now ships the README-linked design. Physical erasure requires directory fsync and explicitly refuses unsupported Windows durability before deleting bytes; ordinary metadata uses file fsync and atomic replacement with the documented Windows directory-flush limit."
  "2026-10-07T21:31:37.979Z",codex-sol,"Independent storage-security review reproduced a retained-byte defect: after staging and committing a unique synthetic binary, its compressed loose-object representation was stored as another valid orphan blob. Obliteration reported success, but inflating the surviving blob and parsing the old frame recovered the exact erased payload. Required correction: scan every surviving object payload for supported raw/framed/zlib/base64 copies before durable denial and refuse ambiguous retained copies; arrival denial must recognize old object-frame digests as well as raw payload digests. Add byte-scan and stale-wrapper arrival regressions. The earlier forged-commit tombstone case now rejects before ref publication."
  "2026-10-07T21:32:12.753Z",codex-sol-implementation,"Storage review found a valid orphan blob retaining an erased loose-object frame through zlib. Extending the erasure plan to inspect every surviving physical object payload before any denial or deletion and refuse ambiguous copies. Arrival denial will recursively compare both full-frame object IDs and type-independent payload digests. Recognizable supported encodings that exceed bounded inspection will fail closed. Adding raw framed, zlib framed and base64 framed regressions plus byte-scan receipts."
  "2026-10-07T21:37:25.331Z",codex-sol-implementation,"Wrapped loose-object reproduction now refuses with erasure_retained_copy, erasureClaimedSuccess=false, recoverable=true and denialPersisted=false. Tracked tests cover raw/compressed/base64 framed orphan copies, preservation on refusal, explicit copy removal, successful negative decoded byte scan, unrelated bytes preserved, and rejected new attributed writes/bundles before storage. Supported representation inspection is bounded and fails closed. All six new production modules and command registration currently measure 100 percent focused lines/statements/functions/branches without exclusions."
  "2026-10-07T21:43:01.917Z",codex-sol,"Independent shared-instance review scheduled a real registration at the boundary between erasure scope discovery and its writer lease. Erasure reported success and persisted denial, but the newly registered working instance retained the exact synthetic payload. Required correction: discover and inventory instances inside the writer transaction and serialize complete registration/unlink/materialization with erasure. Extend regressions to application writers so a successful receipt cannot exclude a supported concurrent worktree operation."
  "2026-10-07T21:43:33.927Z",codex-sol-implementation,"Instance registration review exposed discovery outside the erasure lease, allowing a newly materialized shared instance to retain selected bytes. Moving discovery inside the store transaction and serializing complete registration/unlink/materialization and supported worktree writers. Shared ObjectStore handles for one physical root need synchronous common-lease reentrancy; cross-process exclusion must remain exclusive. Adding a deterministic transaction-boundary regression and checking view, restore and merge marker writes."
  "2026-10-07T21:46:48.409Z",codex-sol,"Independent native-merge acceptance found two feature interactions using real trackers and commits. After erasing one identity, unrelated clean text edits refused with unattributed_arrival because merge output omitted known FileId provenance. Divergent link pin updates attempted blob diff3 and raised object_type_mismatch. Required correction: carry native merge/rewrite provenance without weakening denial, and make incompatible typed link updates an explicit atomic conflict before refs or private layers change; add regressions and documentation."
  "2026-10-07T21:51:48.656Z",codex-sol,"Independent verification of all reproduced feature interactions now passes: forged structural denial refuses incomplete_bundle before ref publication; recoverable compressed object wrappers refuse erasure_retained_copy before denial; late shared-instance registration is included in successful cleanup with recoverable=false; clean unrelated edits merge after erasure; competing link pins refuse link_merge_conflict. These checks used real scratch trackers and native repository operations. Final approval still requires tracked behavioral revert proof and exact-HEAD npm/Bun release gates."
  "2026-10-07T21:54:44.985Z",codex-sol-implementation,"Registration reproduction now reports successful erasure with recoverable=false and one registered instance. Discovery and complete native worktree/ref mutations hold one synchronous store lease; different handles share reentrancy while real child processes remain excluded. Registration publishes recovery scope before materializing payloads and cleans its entry after failed creation cleanup. Merge/replay output now carries reconciled FileId provenance for blob, record and PM-history merges. Competing typed link descriptors raise link_merge_conflict before ref/index/layer mutation; one-sided or agreed changes retain typed links. These are feature fixes, not SDK defects."
  "2026-10-07T22:05:35.772Z",codex-sol-implementation,"Registration and erasure now share one application transaction: scope discovery occurs under the store lease, instances register before copying, and distinct synchronous store handles reuse the same physical-root lease. Real child-process contention refuses before materialization; restore, sparse widening and merge-marker writes cannot publish cached bytes across concurrent erasure. Native merge/replay output carries reconciled FileIds for blobs, records and histories; conflicting link pins refuse atomically as link_merge_conflict. Independent registration, merge, wrapper and structural-denial reproductions pass. Standalone commit/tree bundle arrivals also validate structural closure before storage."
  "2026-10-07T22:06:49.892Z",codex-sol,"Independent shared-instance verification found one classification gap: deleting a held payload produces missing in the hub, but the shared-store reader translates that absence to missing_fragment and the new closure report labels it corrupt. The same physical absence must remain missing across both handles. Add a real linked-instance regression and include missing_fragment in the missing classification before final verification. This is an engine bug, not an SDK defect."
  "2026-10-07T22:12:49.792Z",codex-sol,"Independent decoded-byte scan found a generated-audit leak: erasing a payload whose exact bytes equal the bounded reason incident reports success, but the newly persisted tombstone retains those bytes. Required correction: preflight proposed typed audit frame, durable denial metadata and operation receipt before any write, refusing ambiguous selected content without deleting bytes or publishing denial. Add a regression for refusal, safe-reason retry and zero decoded matches, plus a behavioral revert proof. The separate linked-instance missing_fragment classification also requires correction before final HEAD verification."
  "2026-10-07T22:18:50.853Z",codex-sol-implementation,"Audit leak fixed: canonical tombstone frame, pending/completed denial JSON and planned receipt are inspected before the first audit or denial write; the exact assigned operation receipt is validated under its log lock. Conflicting selected bytes refuse erasure_audit_conflict without deleting bytes or persisting denial. Real reason/timestamp regressions retry with safe metadata and scan every raw/decoded storage file to zero matches. Shared hub/instance missing payloads now both classify missing; damaged bytes remain corrupt and validated absence remains obliterated. All seven behavior-only revert receipts produce exit 1 assertions with modules loaded, including the new audit preflight proof; the behavior is restored. No SDK defect was found."
  "2026-10-07T22:23:13.761Z",codex-sol-implementation,"Linked PM tests ran with progress using schema PM context and the source workspace: node --test test/composition.test.ts passed 37/37; node --test test/composition-consumer.test.ts passed 1/1 and exercised built Node, npm-packed Node and native Bun consumers. Automatic linked-test result tracking is disabled in this tracker, so this comment records the sanitized results. Typecheck, build:test, ESLint, zero-duplication and docstrings pass; native TOON, stat-cache acceptance, production audit and approved Git-identity audit pass. Full source coverage and exact-HEAD release gates remain separate final checks."
  "2026-10-07T22:25:14.290Z",codex-sol-implementation,"Immutable identities now initialize lazily under the common lease and an established identity cannot be overwritten by importing another archive, even into an empty repository. Fresh empty clones adopt the source identity before explicit creation. Erasure validates every stored commit closure, including unreachable history, before mutation; missing structure safely refuses. Link resolution holds both local publication and target-read leases, including self-targeted pins. Built consumers follow the existing child-coverage isolation helper; coverage remains measured through source engine imports with the original all-source thresholds."
  "2026-10-07T22:37:09.791Z",codex-sol-implementation,"Final adversarial fixes are covered by real native regressions: audit-compatible payloads refuse before tombstone/denial publication and preserve old bytes, then safe authorized retry scans clean; shared missing_fragment is classified as missing while damaged bytes remain corrupt. Seven behavior-only revert receipts each exit 1 with an assertion failure and successful module loading, including audit preflight. Additional real filesystem and legacy/fragmented checkout regressions close measured coverage gaps; no thresholds, SDK behavior, or ignores changed. Typecheck, test typecheck, ESLint, zero duplication and 274 documented declarations pass. Full source coverage is running before final regeneration."
  "2026-10-07T22:38:32.828Z",codex-sol-implementation,"Independent scratch reproductions rerun against current source with real trackers: audit-review refuses erasure_audit_conflict with recoverable old bytes and no denial; wrapped-review refuses erasure_retained_copy with no denial; registration-review completes with recoverable=false and the late registered instance included; tombstone-review refuses incomplete_bundle and publishes no ref; shared-missing-review reports missing and no corruption for both hub and instance; merge-review allows unrelated post-erasure merge and refuses competing pins with link_merge_conflict; overlay-review preserves bytes through restore, view and conflicting merge. Tracked behavioral regressions cover these scenarios. README now states precisely that layer removal restores underlying bytes, so desired changes must be reapplied before deliberate staging."
  "2026-10-07T22:39:29.848Z",codex-sol-implementation,"Revert-proof receipts (each reverted only one production behavior, preserved tests/imports, exited 1 with AssertionError, and loaded modules successfully): target identity validation -> committed links retain exact identity; bulk layer masking -> private tracked and new overlays; physical deletion -> authorized erasure scrubs historical; arrival denial -> recoverable loose-frame wrappers; structural denial -> tombstones cannot launder; audit preflight -> proposed audit metadata; retained-copy inspection -> recoverable loose-frame wrappers. Each exact command was node --test --test-name-pattern=\"<listed pattern>\" test/composition.test.ts. Identity/masking/deletion failures were observable byte/index assertion differences; the four refusal checks failed with Missing expected exception. Production behavior was restored after every run. Existing proof receipts remain valid; the additional audit proof demonstrates the reported metadata leak is caught."
  "2026-10-07T22:40:42.503Z",codex-sol-implementation,"pm test pm-vcs-8xis --run --progress passed all three linked commands with zero failures/skips: node --test test/composition.test.ts (41/41 real SDK source scenarios), node --test test/composition-consumer.test.ts (1/1 acceptance test exercising built Node, npm-packed Node and npm-packed Bun), and node --test test/self-host.test.ts (51/51). Linked commands use schema PM context and the source workspace, while each scenario creates its own real disposable tracker. Project automatic test-result tracking is disabled; this comment records the actual sanitized results without changing that policy. The packed consumer verifies the README-linked design ships in package.files. Independent native TOON, stat-cache, production dependency audit and identity audit gates also passed; no SDK defect was found."
  "2026-10-07T22:47:53.228Z",codex-sol,"Final independent lifecycle review reproduced two remaining edge cases for orchestrator correction before PR publication. Canonical incoming denial JSON accepts null/boolean principal or reason fields and persists them despite the string contract. Erasing an empty file then blocks a normal empty-tree commit with object_obliterated, although that existing structural tree still verifies healthy. Add strict string checks at the audit codec boundary and avoid treating zero-byte structural payloads as erased file data; exact denied object IDs and FileIds must remain terminal. Real scratch trackers reproduced both cases. These are engine issues, not SDK bugs."
  "2026-10-07T22:56:21.674Z",codex-sol-implementation,"Implementation is complete and ready for independent review. Final APIs: Repository.identity/setAuthority/stageLink/links/resolveLink, layers/addLayer/removeLayer, readFileState/obliteratedPaths/verify/obliterate; CLI authority, link, link resolve, layer and obliterate. All 930 full-suite tests passed with zero failures/skips. The initial full-source branch result was 99.97%; the only uncovered path was a healthy non-manifest historical read. Added real hub/shared assertions of its blob type and exact bytes, reran the linked 41-scenario source command successfully, and retained unchanged-production full-suite V8 data while executing that scenario under c8 --clean=false --all --100 with the same source includes/excludes: all four dimensions are now 100%. This cumulative diagnostic does not replace the mandatory clean npm and Bun release gates at final HEAD. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, zero duplication, all 274 docstrings, byte scans, built/packed consumers and seven behavioral revert receipts pass. All changed implementation/tests/docs and generated artefacts are linked. No SDK bug was found and no out-of-scope defect requires a follow-up. Shipped limits: loose-store representations only, unknown storage/copies refuse; Windows physical erasure refuses unsupported directory durability; target resolution uses explicit local bindings; external backups/media/custom encryption and direct hostile filesystem writes are outside the application boundary. Releasing the claim while leaving this item in_progress; all PM writes precede changelog/bundle generation and the single SteveBot commit. Exact-HEAD clean gates will be reported in the final handoff."
  "2026-10-07T23:04:39.314Z",codex-sol,"Final lifecycle regressions first failed as observable assertions on loaded modules: malformed inbound principal/reason accepted, and empty-file erasure blocked a healthy empty-tree commit. Strict string guards and nonempty representation digest matching now preserve typed audits and exact erased payload identity without denying empty structure. Individual behavioral reverts each reproduce the assertions; restored source passes. Added path-not-found classification evidence for hub and shared instances to complete the unchanged all-source branch coverage gate."
  "2026-10-07T23:05:42.891Z",codex-sol,"Verification receipt: node --test test/composition.test.ts test/composition-consumer.test.ts passed 44/44 real-tracker scenarios, including built Node, npm-packed Node and native Bun consumers. pm test pm-vcs-8xis --run --progress passed all three linked suites (composition, consumers and self-host); tracker policy disables automatic result recording, so this sanitized receipt records the outcome. Typecheck, build:test, lint, zero-duplication and docstring gates passed. Nine isolated behavioral reverts produced loaded-module assertion failures and were restored. Final exact-HEAD npm and Bun release checks follow the required PM/changelog/staging/bundle/single-commit order; receipts will be attached to the PR."
  "2026-10-07T23:20:02.068Z",codex-sol,"Typed-boundary review extended the audit regression to coercible JSON arrays and reproduced missing string checks for tombstone FileId and committed link repository/revision. Both loaded-module tests failed as Missing expected exception before correction. Explicit string checks now precede identity regex validation; rejected arrivals preserve the object inventory, index, refs and denial registry. These are native engine validation gaps, not SDK defects. The earlier npm release gate passed 932 tests at its previous candidate HEAD; final npm/Bun gates will be rerun after regeneration on the corrected single commit."
  "2026-10-07T23:21:44.955Z",codex-sol,"Final corrected-source verification: 45/45 composition and consumer scenarios passed, including real built Node, npm-packed Node and native Bun. pm test pm-vcs-8xis --run --progress passed all three linked commands (44 composition, 1 consumer, 51 self-host scenarios); automatic recording remains disabled by existing policy. Twelve isolated production-behavior reverts were rerun and each exited 1 with AssertionError and successful module loading: identity pin, layer masking, physical deletion, arrival denial, structural role, audit preflight, retained copy, audit string type, empty structure, FileId string type, link repository string type and link revision string type. All source was restored and positive linked tests passed. Typecheck, build:test, lint, zero duplication and docstrings passed. The final required regeneration and exact-HEAD npm/Bun release receipts are supplied in the PR."
  "2026-10-08T01:30:34.661Z",codex-sol,"Rebased PR 97 onto main after PR 96. Resolving composition and erasure mutations through WorktreeMutation while preserving shared writer locks, FileId metadata, nested control exclusions and root-canonical leaf-link protection. Will verify race, control, composition and byte-scan suites before exact-head release gates."
  "2026-10-08T01:34:20.633Z",codex-sol,"Conflict resolution combines WorktreeMutation-backed checkout and restore with shared erasure locks and FileId/copy provenance. Private layer add/remove, typed descriptor writes, sparse view changes and per-instance obliteration removals use the mutation layer; raw deletion remains only for inventoried control-store objects. Composition rejects case variants of .pmvcs at all depths. Expanded race regression tests pass 226/226 on pinned and portable backends. Fixed store-lock cleanup so root replacement preserves the original refusal and cannot delete a foreign replacement lock."
  "2026-10-08T01:36:33.088Z",codex-sol,"Linked race/control/composition command passed through pm test: 282 tests, zero failures/skips, including the original byte-scan regressions and packed Node/Bun consumer acceptance. Added a further forged nested control-path erasure regression and documented both mutation backends. Typecheck, lint, duplicate, docstring and physical Git identity checks pass. Full coverage and exact committed npm, Bun and isolated-HOME release gates remain pending."
  "2026-10-08T01:38:58.454Z",codex-sol,"Final linked integration receipt: node --expose-gc --test test/worktree-races.test.ts test/control-directories.test.ts test/composition*.test.ts passes 283/283 with zero skips or failures, including expanded composition races, forged nested-control ownership refusal, byte scans and packed consumers. Implementation and documentation are complete. Releasing the claim before freezing PM state, generating CHANGELOG.md and selfhost.bundle, and amending the single PR commit. Push is conditional on npm, Bun and isolated-HOME release checks at the final committed head with 100 percent in all four coverage dimensions. The portable backend retains its documented final-check/use race."
  "2026-10-08T01:44:31.509Z",codex-sol,Preliminary full coverage exposed a CLI contract branch newly bypassed because WorktreeMutation now types a widened-file collision. Added a real control-metadata publication fault regression to prove vcs view still preserves operational I/O errors and releases its writer lock. Earlier source edits during preliminary instrumentation invalidated the composition coverage mapping; final release gates will use frozen committed source.
  "2026-10-08T01:45:15.725Z",codex-sol,"Final supplemental validation passes 284/284 race, control and composition tests with no skips or failures. A frozen-source c8 run limited to engine/composition.ts reports 100/100/100/100; this is component coverage, not the full release denominator. The real view.json directory collision confirms raw metadata I/O errors remain visible and the store lock is released. Typecheck and lint pass. Freeze tracker and source now; regenerate artifacts before the exact-head full release gates."
  "2026-10-10T03:29:18.928Z",codex-sol,"PR97 review follow-up: verify all seven inline findings and the outside-diff Lore finding against the current candidate. Add real filesystem and subprocess regressions before production changes, preserve native-store erasure boundaries, and prove behavior fails on revert. Companion context: pm-cli-website-session-2026-10-10. No dependency refresh unless a verified candidate requires it."
  "2026-10-10T03:34:41.640Z",codex-sol,"All PR97 review bodies, seven inline findings, the outside-diff finding and discussion were read. Filesystem baseline regressions reproduce six runtime issues: legacy fast credential hashes, ordinary file scan limits, 80 denial-file opens for 40 reads, read-only lock contention, unnecessary adoption inventory, and missing ordinary crash recovery. The credential security pass traced both authorize callers (link resolution and obliteration); versioned scrypt grants and validated constant-time comparison will require explicit legacy grant regeneration. Representation scanning must retain encoded-copy and malformed/decompression/nesting refusal; replace raw-size and aggregate-token limits with input-scaled decode accounting rather than skipping privacy inspection."
  "2026-10-10T03:39:53.588Z",codex-sol,"Initial fixes retain supported-encoding inspection and exact denial checks, source coverage and timing gates. New grants use fixed scrypt N=16384/r=8/p=1, 16-byte salt and constant-time 32-byte verifier comparison; legacy grants require explicit regeneration. Denial indexes refresh on device/inode/mtimeNs/ctimeNs/size and records are immutable. Identity advertisement/export is lock-free and does not initialize legacy sources. Adoption avoids full inventory; invalid compression is typed corrupt_object. Ordinary recovery is standalone, pending denial remains authorized, and a syscall regression first proved the old lease publishes an empty owner window. New writer leases atomically hard-link fsynced owner metadata, while aged legacy empty locks have explicit recovery."
  "2026-10-10T03:44:03.731Z",codex-sol,"Focused production regressions pass 9/9, including real strace evidence: 40 reads plus denial lookups open denials.json once (baseline 80 opens), and writer owner bytes precede atomic link publication. The initial full-suite diagnostic exposes old clone fixtures depending on advertisement silently creating identity. Fixtures now request source identity explicitly where clone-stable identity is asserted; separate legacy-source acceptance asserts advertisement/export leave identity absent. Malformed recognizable zlib/framing and excessive nesting continue to refuse by design, preserving the erasure privacy boundary."
  "2026-10-10T03:46:19.046Z",codex-sol,"Boundary review reproduced two corrupt-control gaps within the affected identity/denial readers: an existing JSON null identity was treated as absent and could be replaced; a JSON null denial registry was treated as no denials. The real filesystem regression failed with Missing expected exception separately before each correction. Existing null files now raise typed bad_identity/bad_tombstone rather than resetting immutable identity or reopening payload reads. No new capability or dependency is needed."
  "2026-10-10T04:04:50.954Z",codex-sol,"All twelve behavioral reverts produced nonzero exits with AssertionError and successful module loading; each production change was restored. Real native race tests also pass 4/4: dead-owner disappearance/replacement and same-inode owner edits, pre-publication permission failure leaving known owner metadata, cumulative decode exhaustion, and recovery preserving pending denial/first attribution. strace only pauses native syscalls; filesystem contents, process liveness, syscall results and errno are real. Packed acceptance now checks version 2 grants, ordinary recovery and unchanged legacy identity under built Node, packed Node and native Bun."
  "2026-10-10T04:17:09.061Z",codex-sol,"Linked PM integration passed: node --expose-gc --test test/worktree-races.test.ts test/control-directories.test.ts test/composition*.test.ts test/objects.test.ts test/credentials.test.ts ran 318/318 with zero failures/skips. This includes native lifecycle, root/leaf and writer/crash races, real installed SDK consumers under built Node, npm-packed Node and native Bun. Thirteen behavioral reverts all exit nonzero with AssertionError and loaded modules; sources restored. The last diagnostic recovery read-error branch was verified through real post-stat disappearance. Full unchanged all-source release gates will run at the committed candidate head. Runtime Node 24.19.0, Bun 1.3.5, pinned CLI/SDK 2026.10.4; no dependency changes required."
  "2026-10-10T04:26:11.236Z",codex-sol,"Final atomic-owner check reproduced a real short-write defect with a subprocess RLIMIT_FSIZE one byte below the PID length: writeSync returned a partial owner and the callback ran. The filesystem regression failed before the correction. Lease metadata now uses the native complete-write API before fsync and hard-link publication; the same real limit returns EFBIG, publishes no lease and never runs the callback. Its behavior revert fails with AssertionError. Fourteen verified reverts total; no filesystem results or errno are mocked. The resource-limited child cannot write a valid V8 coverage file, so coverage collection is disabled only for that child; normal full metadata publication is exercised in the parent suite."
  "2026-10-10T04:31:28.644Z",codex-sol,"Final linked integration after complete owner writes passes 319/319, zero failures/skips: node --expose-gc --test test/worktree-races.test.ts test/control-directories.test.ts test/composition*.test.ts test/objects.test.ts test/credentials.test.ts. Built Node, npm-packed Node and native Bun all accept links, layers, version 2 authority, ordinary recovery, readonly legacy identity and intentional absence. Fourteen loaded-module behavioral reverts fail with AssertionError and are restored. Docs and full changelog are updated/generated; final committed-head release:check will retain all source, coverage and production timing gates. Review dispositions: six runtime fixes plus pack-purge/Lore corrections; ordinary size/token scan failures fixed, while malformed encodings and bounded decode refusal intentionally remain for privacy."
  "2026-10-10T05:03:44.269Z",codex-sol,"Exact committed-head release:check ran 1185 tests with zero failures/skips; statements, functions and lines are 100 percent. Strict branches stopped at 99.98 percent on the optional repository identity in HTTP advertisement. Adding a real served-repository regression for both legacy identity absence without mutation and an explicit immutable identity. No production gate or threshold changes; rerun the full exact-head gate after committing this acceptance evidence."
  "2026-10-10T05:05:19.333Z",codex-sol,Real HTTP acceptance passes both legacy identity absence without mutation and explicitly established identity with unchanged refs/config. Reverting readonly advertisement to identity initialization fails that test with AssertionError; restored source. Fifteen behavioral fail-on-revert proofs now pass their failure checks. The new linked HTTP test passed 1/1 with zero failures/skips. Committing acceptance evidence with matching PM history and regenerated selfhost bundle; final full release gate will run at the new exact head.
  "2026-10-10T05:42:48.042Z",codex-sol,"Renewed PR97 review resumes at 32324d1627cc3051e2c3594b9d068ee603e30eae. Verify all nine inline findings and the undo/reset outside-diff descriptions against real source and filesystem behavior. Prioritize manifest merge integrity, private-layer mutation preflight and retired-instance binding. Preserve corruption/closure and encoded-denial guarantees while measuring repeated reads and ordinary no-op sync. Existing 1186-test release receipt remains the prior-head baseline; no new owner, no upstream or companion changes, no review replies."
  "2026-10-10T05:50:40.451Z",codex-sol,"Verified renewed data-integrity findings against loaded modules and real storage. Six switch/reset/undo/rebase scenarios failed with changed HEAD/ref/index/oplog state; a retired path reused by an independent clone was actually erased before the binding guard. Manifest-kind matrices now preserve an existing side and return per-path content conflicts. The base64-zlib suggested catch would silently certify a recoverable encoded denied marker when inflation exceeds the decode budget; retain strict refusal and prove the marker is found with sufficient inspection budget. Performance baseline: link listing read 4195608 compressed bytes for a 4 MiB unrelated payload; no-op fetch walked held history. New real strace tests target bounded prefix listing, metadata-only sync and one layer snapshot per operation. No gate thresholds or fixture deadlines changed."
  "2026-10-10T05:59:14.951Z",codex-sol,"Focused integration passed 193/193 with zero failures/skips; its selected eight-file coverage is diagnostic only, not the 53-file release denominator. Corrected test-authoring fixture errors (manifest return shape, series author/schema and a nonexistent inventory method) are excluded from behavioral red evidence. Corrected regressions pass 25/25 before two additional path/I/O cases. Native traces: cold no-op validates 14 held objects once, 4199457/4199457 compressed bytes and zero source loose opens; unrelated 4 MiB link content reads 64 compressed bytes; shared import with two FileIds plus series base/patch and ref reads one 262245-byte compressed payload. Preserve no-op corruption refusal: constant-byte cold sync is explicitly not claimed. A corrected real held-duplicate arrival test failed with AssertionError before adding full held-copy verification; restored import refuses before refs or inventory change. Stale canonical reports were removed after source changes; final all-source coverage remains pending."
  "2026-10-10T06:04:51.938Z",codex-sol,"All 27 renewed scenarios pass; the linked command node --test --test-name-pattern=renewed test/composition.test.ts passed through pm test --run --only-last --progress. Nineteen isolated source-only reversions each exit 1 with AssertionError and successful module loading; every production file was restored. The writer case was repeated after preloading its real waiting process, preserving the ten-second child bound and proving that a live lease lasting 2.5 seconds succeeds only with the corrected production wait. Prune authority, still-bound scope refusal and local audit recording have separate fail-on-revert proofs. Production inventory remains exactly 53 source files (no new production files), Node 24.19.0/native Bun 1.3.5, installed SDK 2026.10.4 and actual Node types 26.6.4. Final unchanged all-source release gate, LCOV inventory, packed consumer acceptance and PM history verification follow."
  "2026-10-10T06:07:19.066Z",codex-sol,"Built Node, npm-packed Node and native Bun consumer acceptance passed 1/1, including the new authorized prune command and its audit. The base64-zlib regression now also uses a real 20 MiB historical payload, authorized erasure and a later encoded arrival: default inspection refuses before publishing bytes, and sufficient-budget inspection identifies the recoverable payload. All nine inline IDs and outside-diff review 5477799727 are dispositioned in docs/links-layers-obliteration.md. Unsafe presence-only closure trust and blanket base64-derived inflate-error suppression are rejected with concrete corruption/encoded-copy evidence; cold no-op remains one complete receiver byte pass and malformed recognizable encodings remain conservative refusal. Preparing a committed candidate with the existing 53-file source inventory and nineteen source-only assertion-failure proofs; no skips, threshold changes, hosted or upstream edits."
  "2026-10-10T06:21:05.564Z",codex-sol,"Committed candidate f934a05e3abbeba1f22c4f873c5a38b672e81831 ran the complete 1213-test suite: 1213 passed, zero failed/skipped/canceled. The strict release gate stopped at 99.98 percent branches; statements/functions/lines were 100 percent across all 53 LCOV source files, with exactly one zero-hit branch (legacy metadata fallback in engine/sync.ts). Failed canonical reports were invalidated and retained only as diagnostic evidence. Independent compatibility inspection found that HttpTransport always exposes fetchObjects although object-fetch is optional in peer advertisements. A real loopback proxy advertising a legacy peer without that capability reproduced a no-op HTTP failure with AssertionError. The source now respects the advertised capability and uses the existing bundle fallback. This is a related compatibility fix and missing acceptance evidence; the final gate will rerun after committing it, with unchanged thresholds and deadlines."
  "2026-10-10T06:28:26.121Z",codex-sol,"Renewed linked acceptance now passes 28/28 with zero failures, skips or cancellations: node --test --test-name-pattern=renewed test/composition.test.ts test/served-sync.test.ts, executed through pm test --run --only-last --progress. Two additional production-only reversions prove the advertised legacy HTTP capability fallback and physical shared-control-directory binding before a foreign repository configuration can be opened. Total isolated proof cases are 21/21 nonzero assertion failures with successfully loaded modules; restored source passes. Typecheck, lint and docstring gate pass, covering 53 production files and 283 documented declarations. Two promise-executor lint errors in the new HTTP fixture were corrected with explicit void executor bodies; they were test-authoring defects, not behavioral evidence. The 53-file production inventory and all strict coverage thresholds remain unchanged. Preparing the immutable final candidate and linked complete release gate; the earlier 1213-test branch-coverage failure remains recorded, with failed reports invalidated."
  "2026-10-10T06:46:53.533Z",codex-sol,"Root renewal: exact-head GitHub CodeQL114154266078 flags SSRF in new legacy-peer test relay test/served-sync.test.ts:753. The relay derives upstream URL from incoming request.url, so an absolute request target can override its loopback fixture origin. This is a test-only URL boundary, not a demonstrated production endpoint finding. Add a real bounded local absolute-target rejection case first; require it to fail old fixture then restrict forwarding to two statically built local endpoints. Production source bytes and prior4f3144f full1214/four100 receipt remain unchanged; new-head CI and reviewers must rerun."
  "2026-10-10T06:59:26.175Z",codex-sol,"Root repaired CodeQL27/inline4236742733 in legacy HTTP test relay: incoming request targets no longer construct upstream URLs; only statically built known loopback advertise/fetch endpoints forward. Real POST absolute-target request returns200 with unsafe original forwarding and404 after repair; normal negative-only source control exits1 with actual200/expected404, without forced-exit flag. Earlier accidental GET baseline threw in advertisement parsing and timed out during teardown, so it is rejected as behavioral proof. Fixed fixture drains unknown requests, disables raw client pooling and closes listener before its sockets. Real ordinary positive1/1 and all28 PM-linked renewed cases pass with normal cleanup; typecheck/build:test/lint pass. All53 production bytes are unchanged from accepted4f3144f1214/four100; new-head CI and source-memory/upload-order review repairs still required. Existingowner staysopen; no tenant/core/hosted/telemetry changes."
  "2026-10-10T07:00:53.900Z",codex-sol,"Renewed review follow-up on the existing feature branch: preserve root relay repair and dated accepted receipt; verify recovery authorization ordering, bounded export discovery, held closure leaf retention, and batch hash ordering with real source-only negative proofs. Keep immutable integrity and denials under one lease; run the strict complete release gate before branch-only push and handoff. No closure or GitHub feedback actions."
  "2026-10-10T07:07:03.192Z",codex-sol,All four renewed findings verified by original-source assertion failures. Corrected the memory fixture type and invalid short ChangeId before accepting its red evidence; corrected typecheck access to shared authority scope. Baseline export read 8391216 bytes for a 4195608-byte compressed leaf. Baseline closure kept 149097462 buffer bytes for 134217728 payload bytes; restored source measured 14878192 buffer growth and 19529728 native peak RSS growth with all 64 leaves physically read once. Recovery and upload ordering also fail original source and pass restored source. No gate thresholds or deadlines changed; canonical reports invalidated after source edits. Keep prior accepted source and relay receipts dated.
  "2026-10-10T07:11:46.804Z",codex-sol,"Root exact20d757c CI38032850029 failure diagnosed: Node22/26 coverage/native gates pass, but accept:self-host correctly rejects three committed differences: test/served-sync.test.ts plus8xis toon/history. Root omitted selfhost.bundle regeneration after test/PM relay change. This is rejected complete-CI evidence; CodeQL is green. Upcoming source-repair candidate must stage all tests/docs/PM metadata, regenerate selfhost.bundle, commit immutable source, then repeat full gate and compare committed byte equality without expanding exclusions. Existing four100 receipt remains4f3144f only; do not accept20d ascomplete release."
